<title>GREECE: GREEK BROKERS EXPECT PASOK TO WIN ELECTIONS- FLASH RADIO POLL.</title>
<headline>GREEK BROKERS EXPECT PASOK TO WIN ELECTIONS- FLASH RADIO POLL.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The majority of Greek brokers</p>
<p>expect the socialist PASOK party of Costas Simitis to prevail in</p>
<p>national elections on September 22 according to a poll by Flash</p>
<p>radio station.</p>
<p>Flash polled 64 of the total 66 Athens stock exchange member</p>
<p>firms asking the respective chief executive to name the</p>
<p>political party that would win the elections. There were 54</p>
<p>responses from the sample of 64 brokerages. The results have as</p>
<p>follows:</p>
<p>    Brokers see win by:    PASOK 21  --   New Democracy 3</p>
<p>    To close to call:		    20</p>
<p>    Don't know/won't answer:	   10</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
